\section{Aether Genome Interface System Overview}
\label{sec:aether-genome-interface}

\subsection{System Identity and Scope}
The \textbf{Aether Genome Interface} (AGI) is a sovereign, multi-domain analysis framework
designed to fuse encrypted astrophysical telemetry, biocryptographic complexity mapping,
and high-entropy distributed computation into a single coherent pipeline. Its primary
objective is to enable anomaly triage and complexity classification across large-scale
cosmic datasets without imposing anthropocentric biological assumptions.

Core design principles:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Non-anthropic inference:} Avoids Earth-centric life templates; focuses on complexity, structure, and statistical deviation.
    \item \textbf{Cryptographic integrity:} All data streams are processed under high-entropy cipher regimes with verified packet fidelity.
    \item \textbf{Distributed resilience:} Sovereign kernel architecture maintains consensus and stability under node failure and overload.
    \item \textbf{Instrument anchoring:} Ingest layers are explicitly tied to real or realistic observatory profiles (e.g., ALMA, Cygnus-region targets).
\end{itemize}

