\subsection{Functional Role in Astrobiological Inference}
The AGI does not claim direct detection of extraterrestrial biology. Instead, it provides:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Complexity triage:} Identification of statistically significant anomalies
    in spectral, structural, and cryptographic domains.
    \item \textbf{Non-anthropic classification:} Ranking of signals by complexity and
    deviation without forcing Earth-like biological templates.
    \item \textbf{Instrument-anchored diagnostics:} Integration of real observatory
    profiles (e.g., ALMA, KELT-9b) to keep inference grounded in physical data.
\end{itemize}
In this sense, the Aether Genome Interface is a \emph{meta-inference engine}: it
evaluates where the universe exhibits unusual structure or behavior, while maintaining
strict cryptographic and statistical discipline across all layers of the pipeline.